WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:32.500
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.750
<b>that He had created the varna system,</b>

3
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.708
<b>but He Himself is not a </b>
<b>character within this system,</b>

4
00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:44.458
<b>nor does He undergo any </b>
<b>change due to this system.</b>

5
00:00:44.458 --> 00:00:47.791
<b>Now in this verse, Lord Krishna clarifies</b>

6
00:00:47.791 --> 00:00:51.916
<b>why He does not call Himself a </b>
<b>character of this varna system,</b>

7
00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:57.708
<b>and how understanding this truth </b>
<b>about Him is beneficial for mankind.</b>

8
00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:05.958
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna says</b>

9
00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>that “no action binds Me,</b>

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.166
<b>nor do I have any desire for the fruits of action.”</b>

11
00:01:13.166 --> 00:01:21.208
<b>“And whoever understands this truth about Me, </b>
<b>is also not bound by the fruits of their actions.”</b>

12
00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:23.916
<b>What Lord Krishna means to say is</b>

13
00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:27.791
<b>that even though He Himself is </b>
<b>involved in many activities,</b>

14
00:01:27.791 --> 00:01:31.333
<b>but, He is not affected by these activities.</b>

15
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:37.041
<b>Where on one hand, humans perform every </b>
<b>action with the expectation of reward or result,</b>

16
00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:37.750


17
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.458
<b>Lord Krishna does not expect any result.</b>

18
00:01:41.458 --> 00:01:47.708
<b>This is because He is complete </b>
<b>in Himself, always blissful.</b>

19
00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:51.833
<b>And in such a case, what expectation</b>
<b>can He have of any result?</b>

20
00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:56.583
<b>Humans give excessive importance to actions </b>
<b>and their results in their lives.</b>

21
00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.583
<b>And then as a result of these very actions,</b>

22
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:05.500
<b>they experience emotions like </b>
<b>enthusiasm, worry, joy, and sorrow.</b>

23
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.250
<b>But</b>

24
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.708
<b> Lord Krishna performs actions not for any result,</b>

25
00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:12.958
<b>but only out of love and a sense of duty.</b>

26
00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:16.416
<b>And if there was no desire for any result at all,</b>

27
00:02:16.416 --> 00:02:22.541
<b>then declaring that result as good or </b>
<b>bad becomes completely meaningless.</b>

28
00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:27.250
<b>That is why Lord Krishna says </b>
<b>that no action binds Him,</b>

29
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.083
<b>because</b>

30
00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:35.125
<b>no result awakens sorrow or worry in Him, </b>
<b>nor enthusiasm or joy. </b>

31
00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:41.708
<b>From this very statement of Lord Krishna, we too </b>
<b>can take inspiration to act without being affected.</b>

32
00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:43.916
<b>When we adopt this perspective,</b>

33
00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:46.208
<b>we neither get entangled in </b>
<b>the bondage of action,</b>

34
00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:51.291
<b>nor are we affected by the emotional upheaval </b>
<b>of the results of that action.</b>

35
00:02:51.291 --> 00:02:56.291
<b>In such a case, we perform actions, </b>
<b>but without any attachment,</b>

36
00:02:56.291 --> 00:03:00.916
<b>because we believe that only the action </b>
<b>is in our control,</b>

37
00:03:00.916 --> 00:03:02.875
<b>not its result.</b>

38
00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:06.166
<b>The role of Lord Krishna is like that of rain.</b>

39
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:10.583
<b>Rain impartially provides water to all land.</b>

40
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:16.750
<b>Now rain cannot decide which </b>
<b>crop will grow on that land,</b>

41
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:22.375
<b>and for this reason, the result of what</b>
<b> grows there has no effect on the falling of rain.</b>

42
00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:30.666
<b>The crop that will grow on that land depends </b>
<b>solely and only on the seeds sown there.</b>

43
00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:31.791
<b>Similarly,</b>

44
00:03:31.791 --> 00:03:35.625
<b>Lord Krishna gives all humans an </b>
<b>equal and free opportunity</b>

45
00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:41.208
<b>to act according to their desires and </b>
<b>past actions.</b>

46
00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:47.000
<b>But just as the responsibility of the crop depends </b>
<b>on the seed, not on the rain,</b>

47
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.458
<b>similarly</b>

48
00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:53.333
<b>the responsibility of the actions performed </b>
<b>by humans does not lie with Lord Krishna,</b>

49
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:54.208
<b>but</b>

50
00:03:54.208 --> 00:04:00.458
<b>depends on the past actions of that human </b>
<b>and the decisions of the present life.</b>

51
00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:04.250
<b>Despite being the Lord of the entire universe,</b>

52
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:11.208
<b>Lord Krishna performs His actions without </b>
<b>any worry or attachment, merely as a duty.</b>

53
00:04:11.208 --> 00:04:15.583
<b>This thought is not only verbal but also practical,</b>

54
00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:19.041
<b>because the result is not in our control at all.</b>

55
00:04:19.041 --> 00:04:20.833
<b>By following this thought,</b>

56
00:04:20.833 --> 00:04:26.750
<b>we too can perform our duty </b>
<b>without any bondage of action.</b>

57
00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:34.375
<b>No action binds me,</b>

58
00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:35.500
<b>because</b>

59
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:40.083
<b>I have no desire for any result or </b>
<b>fruit from my actions.</b>

60
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:41.333
<b>But</b>

61
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:43.666
<b>humans are not like that.</b>

62
00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:44.750
<b>Generally,</b>

63
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.750
<b>their every action is motivated by results,</b>

64
00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.208
<b>be it the desire for success,</b>

65
00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:56.000
<b>some financial gain, or their identity in society.</b>

66
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.125
<b>And</b>

67
00:04:57.125 --> 00:04:59.916
<b>this very attachment to results,</b>

68
00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:07.208
<b>becomes an endless </b>
<b>cycle of stress, disappointment, and desires.</b>

69
00:05:07.208 --> 00:05:08.791
<b>But,</b>

70
00:05:08.791 --> 00:05:15.083
<b>if you want, just like me, without being </b>
<b>attached to the results,</b>

71
00:05:15.083 --> 00:05:20.708
<b>you too can learn to perform your duties.</b>

72
00:05:20.708 --> 00:05:24.708
<b>Performing your actions without </b>
<b>the desire for the fruit –</b>

73
00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:29.416
<b>this is the essence of ‘nishkam karma yoga.’</b>

74
00:05:29.416 --> 00:05:34.958
<b>Now does this mean that you should </b>
<b>not have any goals in life?</b>

75
00:05:34.958 --> 00:05:35.958
<b>No.</b>

76
00:05:35.958 --> 00:05:37.291
<b>Absolutely not.</b>

77
00:05:37.291 --> 00:05:43.833
<b>It only means that you set </b>
<b>actions to reach that goal,</b>

78
00:05:43.833 --> 00:05:49.791
<b>and then focus your attention only on that action,</b>

79
00:05:49.791 --> 00:05:57.500
<b>not constantly worrying about whether this </b>
<b>action will bring you success or not.</b>

80
00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.208
<b>This worry is futile, isn't it?</b>

81
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:01.666
<b>And also,</b>

82
00:06:01.666 --> 00:06:04.583
<b>whether the result is good or bad,</b>

83
00:06:04.583 --> 00:06:08.291
<b>the only thing in your control is to</b>

84
00:06:08.291 --> 00:06:14.125
<b>make the right decision and take the </b>
<b>next step, do the next action.</b>

85
00:06:14.125 --> 00:06:20.708
<b>This thinking will not disturb your </b>
<b>peace of mind in any result.</b>

86
00:06:20.708 --> 00:06:21.500


87
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.791
<b>How to practically apply this?</b>

88
00:06:25.791 --> 00:06:27.500
<b>First,</b>

89
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:36.125
<b>introspect and know that you are </b>
<b>distressed by such results countless times,</b>

90
00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:41.791
<b>where changing them was perhaps </b>
<b>not even in your hands.</b>

91
00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:50.625
<b>Just as I perform the work of protecting </b>
<b>and guiding this world without any attachment,</b>

92
00:06:50.625 --> 00:06:53.250
<b>you too can do this.</b>

93
00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.500
<b>Helping a family member,</b>

94
00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.458
<b>assisting a colleague,</b>

95
00:06:57.458 --> 00:07:01.291
<b>benefiting a poor or helpless person.</b>

96
00:07:01.291 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>Or even if it is your daily or ordinary work,</b>

97
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:16.208
<b>just try to do that work with a </b>
<b>sense of love, duty, and welfare.</b>

98
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:17.791
<b>Then see,</b>

99
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:22.458
<b>not only will you experience immense </b>
<b>satisfaction in that work,</b>

100
00:07:22.458 --> 00:07:23.375
<b>but</b>

101
00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:27.916
<b>you will also find your spiritual level rising.</b>

102
00:07:27.916 --> 00:07:30.375
<b>Do try this effort.</b>

103
00:07:36.916 --> 00:07:40.166
<b>No action binds me,</b>

104
00:07:40.166 --> 00:07:43.791
<b>nor do I desire any fruit.</b>

105
00:07:43.791 --> 00:07:52.166
<b>I only guide mankind with</b>
<b>a sense of love and duty.</b>

106
00:07:52.166 --> 00:07:57.916
<b>This same perspective can be </b>
<b>helpful for you in family life as well.</b>

107
00:07:57.916 --> 00:08:00.291
<b>Often in a family,</b>

108
00:08:00.291 --> 00:08:06.875
<b>our decisions and our behavior are bound by</b>
<b>the expectation of some result.</b>

109
00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:08.166
<b>For example,</b>

110
00:08:08.166 --> 00:08:09.458
<b>the expectation</b>

111
00:08:09.458 --> 00:08:14.791
<b>that your child will choose their professional</b>
<b>path according to your instructions,</b>

112
00:08:14.791 --> 00:08:21.916
<b>or expecting a particular behavior</b>
<b>from your life partner.</b>

113
00:08:21.916 --> 00:08:23.958
<b>Is this wrong?</b>

114
00:08:23.958 --> 00:08:25.583
<b>No.</b>

115
00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:26.541
<b>But</b>

116
00:08:26.541 --> 00:08:29.250
<b>you also have to understand</b>

117
00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:35.083
<b>that your expectation involves</b>
<b>another family member.</b>

118
00:08:35.083 --> 00:08:42.250
<b>So thinking that someone else should </b>
<b>live their life according to you.</b>

119
00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.958
<b>That's not right, is it?</b>

120
00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:52.083
<b>Definitely guide family members with </b>
<b>a sense of love and duty,</b>

121
00:08:52.083 --> 00:08:54.125
<b>but understand,</b>

122
00:08:54.125 --> 00:08:56.791
<b>they have to live their lives,</b>

123
00:08:56.791 --> 00:09:03.500
<b>and ultimately they will have to choose </b>
<b>the decisions and paths related to life.</b>

124
00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.541
<b>This does not at all mean</b>

125
00:09:05.541 --> 00:09:11.666
<b>that family members cannot have any </b>
<b>opinion about each other's lives.</b>

126
00:09:11.666 --> 00:09:17.333
<b>Taking an interest in each other's lives, </b>
<b>thinking about each other's well-being,</b>

127
00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:20.208
<b>this is the foundation of a family.</b>

128
00:09:20.208 --> 00:09:21.291
<b>But</b>

129
00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:27.041
<b>being someone's well-wisher, </b>
<b>and trying to control their life,</b>

130
00:09:27.041 --> 00:09:31.791
<b>there is a world of difference between these two.</b>

131
00:09:31.791 --> 00:09:35.166
<b>If you are the true well-wisher of family members,</b>

132
00:09:35.166 --> 00:09:38.750
<b>then your approach will always be of cooperation,</b>

133
00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:42.416
<b>not criticism and control.</b>

134
00:09:42.416 --> 00:09:46.750
<b>Understand how to practically implement this.</b>

135
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.500
<b>Begin with mutual discussion,</b>

136
00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:54.375
<b>whenever a family member has to </b>
<b>make an important decision,</b>

137
00:09:54.375 --> 00:09:58.416
<b>discuss it together, give your suggestions,</b>

138
00:09:58.416 --> 00:10:03.041
<b>weigh the positive and negative </b>
<b>aspects of each suggestion.</b>

139
00:10:03.041 --> 00:10:04.791
<b>But in the end,</b>

140
00:10:04.791 --> 00:10:08.375
<b>know that they have to make the decision.</b>

141
00:10:08.375 --> 00:10:14.291
<b>And if they make a decision that</b>
<b>is contrary to your suggestion,</b>

142
00:10:14.291 --> 00:10:17.958
<b>calmly understand their perspective.</b>

143
00:10:17.958 --> 00:10:20.500
<b>And then assure them that in every result,</b>

144
00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.625
<b>good or bad,</b>

145
00:10:22.625 --> 00:10:26.416
<b>you stand with them.</b>

146
00:10:26.416 --> 00:10:27.791
<b>Think,</b>

147
00:10:27.791 --> 00:10:30.916
<b>in matters related to your life,</b>

148
00:10:30.916 --> 00:10:36.833
<b>you would also want such behavior </b>
<b>from family members, right?</b>

149
00:10:36.833 --> 00:10:38.083
<b>Think…</b>

150
00:10:42.791 --> 00:10:45.625
<b>In professional life, it is necessary</b>

151
00:10:45.625 --> 00:10:50.000
<b>that you fulfill your responsibility wholeheartedly,</b>

152
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:50.916
<b>but</b>

153
00:10:50.916 --> 00:10:56.958
<b>without excessive attachment to the result.</b>

154
00:10:56.958 --> 00:10:58.500
<b>Think about</b>

155
00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:01.875
<b>how any result comes.</b>

156
00:11:01.875 --> 00:11:08.000
<b>When people do their work wholeheartedly</b>
<b>towards that result.</b>

157
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.208
<b>Ultimately,</b>

158
00:11:09.208 --> 00:11:14.166
<b>if you look at it, the result is </b>
<b>also a product of hard work.</b>

159
00:11:14.166 --> 00:11:17.333
<b>If your effort is excellent,</b>

160
00:11:17.333 --> 00:11:20.083
<b>the result will automatically improve.</b>

161
00:11:20.083 --> 00:11:21.333
<b>Therefore,</b>

162
00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:25.750
<b>if you are appointed to a leadership </b>
<b>position in an organization,</b>

163
00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:30.541
<b>try to create an environment</b>

164
00:11:30.541 --> 00:11:34.333
<b>where people without being under </b>
<b>excessive pressure of results,</b>

165
00:11:34.333 --> 00:11:40.083
<b>focus on fulfilling their duties</b>
<b>with complete dedication.</b>

166
00:11:40.083 --> 00:11:44.666
<b>There are also some ways to </b>
<b>implement this at the workplace.</b>

167
00:11:44.666 --> 00:11:46.041
<b>First of all,</b>

168
00:11:46.041 --> 00:11:51.666
<b>you will have to become a living example</b>
<b>of this thinking yourself.</b>

169
00:11:51.666 --> 00:11:56.125
<b>Do your every work with complete </b>
<b>dedication and integrity,</b>

170
00:11:56.125 --> 00:11:58.916
<b>emphasize morality more than results.</b>

171
00:11:58.916 --> 00:12:01.583
<b>Only when you follow this,</b>

172
00:12:01.583 --> 00:12:05.083
<b>people will also take this approach seriously.</b>

173
00:12:05.083 --> 00:12:06.416
<b>After that,</b>

174
00:12:06.416 --> 00:12:10.791
<b>whenever there is a discussion on the </b>
<b>goals of the organization with colleagues,</b>

175
00:12:10.791 --> 00:12:13.333
<b>definitely set goals there,</b>

176
00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:14.291
<b>but</b>

177
00:12:14.291 --> 00:12:17.083
<b>more importantly,</b>

178
00:12:17.083 --> 00:12:20.291
<b>explain everyone their workload,</b>

179
00:12:20.291 --> 00:12:24.041
<b>and then monitor the progress of this workload,</b>

180
00:12:24.041 --> 00:12:26.750
<b>not just the results.</b>

181
00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:28.958
<b>There are two benefits of this approach,</b>

182
00:12:28.958 --> 00:12:29.750
<b>first,</b>

183
00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:31.916
<b>people will understand</b>

184
00:12:31.916 --> 00:12:37.708
<b> that you are more interested in the </b>
<b>effort leading there than the result.</b>

185
00:12:37.708 --> 00:12:38.666
<b>Also,</b>

186
00:12:38.666 --> 00:12:43.833
<b>during this monitoring, if any employee </b>
<b>needs any assistance,</b>

187
00:12:43.833 --> 00:12:46.750
<b> you will be able to provide that as well.</b>

188
00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:50.083
<b>You will also be able to plan their training.</b>

189
00:12:50.083 --> 00:12:51.291
<b>And finally,</b>

190
00:12:51.291 --> 00:12:53.083
<b>whatever the result,</b>

191
00:12:53.083 --> 00:12:59.333
<b>regularly appreciate the hard work </b>
<b>and thinking of worthy colleagues.</b>

192
00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:00.625
<b>Remember,</b>

193
00:13:00.625 --> 00:13:04.833
<b>people do not become bad because of bad results.</b>

194
00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:08.833
<b>This very thinking will help you going forward.</b>

